.include {docs}
.doclang {en}

Generated packages include `scripts/bakingrl-plugin.mjs`.

## Global Local Install

Before npm publication, install the SDK repository globally:

```sh
cd BakingRLSDK
npm install
npm install -g .
```

This provides:

```sh
create-bakingrl-plugin
bakingrl-plugin
```

Generated packages use the local SDK checkout through a `file:` dependency.

After editing SDK types or runtime helpers:

```sh
npm run build
```

If you changed the generator, package helper, templates, or global command
metadata:

```sh
npm install -g . --force
```

## Commands

```sh
npm run build
npm run check
npm run add -- visual boostMeter
npm run add -- component PlayerCard
npm run add -- service matchStats
npm run add -- connector twitch
npm run inspect
npm run pack
npm run keygen -- signing-key.json
npm run sign -- --key signing-key.json
npm run install:local
```

## Validate

```sh
node scripts/bakingrl-plugin.mjs validate
```

Validation checks that:

- `bakingrl.plugin.json` exists.
- The schema is `bakingrl.plugin/2`.
- Required package fields are present.
- Export entries point to built `.js` files inside the package.
- Page templates stay inside the package.

## Pack

```sh
node scripts/bakingrl-plugin.mjs pack
```

`pack` writes hashes, then creates a `.brlp` archive in `dist-bundles/`.

## Install Locally

```sh
node scripts/bakingrl-plugin.mjs install-local
```

This copies the package into BakingRL's local app-data package directory.
